# CUTAWAY — seeing a plan while you build it.
#
# ⚠ THE PAIR IS THE CLAIM, AND IT IS THE SAME STANDING POSITION IN BOTH. CUTAWAY is
# not "a nicer picture"; it is *the same author, in the same place, able to see what
# they are editing*. So every row below is FOLLOW and CUTAWAY from one spot, and the
# difference has to be in the frame rather than in where the author walked.

echo --- flat ground
at 0 0 0
verb raise
wait rebuilt

echo --- a house where the author is looking
at 0 -4 90
verb place
wait rebuilt

send 27:1

echo --- FOLLOW, standing in the middle of the floor: a wall and a ceiling
send 40:1
at 0 0 90
step 150
# ⚠ THE BOOM IS THE OTHER HALF OF THE CLAIM, and `cam` alone REPORTS it. Indoors
# FOLLOW is held close by the walls — 2.152 — and CUTAWAY may stand well back because
# it has taken the roof off. The pair is what makes each number mean something.
cam 1.8 2.5
snap s14-follow-in
# The roof's underside is a fifth of the frame and there is no grass in shot: this is
# a room with a ceiling on it.
frame 0 0.85 soffit 0.14 0.26 grass 0 0.001

echo --- CUTAWAY, the SAME spot: roof off, steep, and the plan should be visible
send 40:3
at 0 0 90
step 150
cam 6.0 8.0
snap s14-cutaway-in
# ⚠ THE SAME SPOT, AND THE SOFFIT IS GONE. `soffit 0 0.001` is the whole verb: CUTAWAY
# takes the roof off, so what was overhead is now sky-lit ground. Grass appearing from
# INSIDE is the same fact read the other way, and the frame gets brighter for it.
frame 0 0.90 soffit 0 0.001 grass 0.18 0.35 lum 0.36 0.52

echo --- CUTAWAY from outside, where the whole building should be in shot
at 0 -10 90
step 150
cam 6.0 8.0
snap s14-cutaway-out
frame 0 0.90 grass 0.75 0.92 soffit 0 0.001

echo --- and back to FOLLOW, to prove the mode is not a one-way door
send 40:1
at 0 0 90
step 150
# ⚠ THE SAME NUMBERS AS THE FIRST ROW, WHICH IS WHAT "not a one-way door" MEANS. The
# boom comes back in and the ceiling comes back.
cam 1.8 2.5
# ⛔ THIS ROW HAD NO `snap` AND SO JUDGED THE PREVIOUS STATION'S PICTURE — "a row about
# an unknown scene", by `frame`'s own definition. It has one now.
snap s14-back-to-follow
frame 0 0.85 soffit 0.14 0.26 grass 0 0.001
